# One rule: nothing derived from the game dump, from PS3 firmware, or from a
# build is tracked.  This repository contains only hand-written host code and
# the vendored ps3recomp framework.

# --- Anything produced from the user's own dump -----------------------------
# the dump itself, its VFS mounts, and the patched ELFs
game/
# Ghidra's raw string-table dump is verbatim content excerpted from the
# executable, unlike the address/symbol maps beside it.  It is an output of
# ps3recomp/tools/ghidra_analyze.py and no build step reads it.
ghidra_out/strings.json
gamedata/
# lifted PPU code -- every variant: working snapshot, pristine baselines kept
# for re-deriving hand edits, and any experimental lift
src/recomp*/
# lifted SPU images
src/spu_gen/

# --- Build output and third-party prefixes ----------------------------------
build*/
third_party/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/

# --- Binary formats we must never carry -------------------------------------
*.elf
*.ELF
*.self
*.SELF
*.prx
*.sprx
*.pkg
*.sfo
*.nub
*.rap
*.keys

# --- Diagnostics, captures, logs --------------------------------------------
captures/
*.log
*.rsxb
frame_*.bmp
rt_save.bmp
tex_*.bin
vp_[0-9A-F]*.hlsl
recomp_spu_ls.bin
vkd3d-proton.cache*

# --- Local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Runtime online configuration; holds the pairing token.
taiko_online.cfg

# The overlay font (fonts/font.ttf) IS tracked: the pairing code has to be
# legible out of the box, and the build embeds a subset of it.
